  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1254 PM EDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\n- Light Rain Tonight\n\nTonight sees a mid-level wave track across the area dragging a cold \nfront with it. Compared to yesterday guidance suggests a more robust \nmid-level wave and better moisture quality. This brings at least low \nrain chances as far south as I-96, potentially further south, and \nwarrants scattered PoPs north of approx. M20. \n\n- Several Chances For Frost/Freeze Conditions Next Week\n\nConditions then are favored to remain dry into early next week as \neven with frontal boundaries and several shortwaves persisting in \nnorthwest flow, moisture quality is poor. Will keep the going NBM \ndry forecast given that which keeps conditions dry.\n\nThe main concern is frost, particularly Sunday Night and Monday \nNight. Behind the cold front, 850mb temps fall to around 0C along \nwith a drier airmass and surface high. This will favor ample \nradiational cooling. Sunday Night frost potential will be primarily \nacross the northern CWA similar to this morning. However the coldest \nair arrives Monday Night with lows in the low to mid 30s. More \nwidespread frost is possible with potentially freezing conditions \nacross the northern interior CWA, especially in the known cold \nhollows.",
